{title: Rock of Ages Cleft for Me}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Rock of [**]Ages, [F]cleft for [C]me, let me [G]hide myself in [C]Thee
Let the [G]water [G7]and the [C]blood, from Thy [G]wounded [G7]side which [C]flowed
Be of [C]sin the [F]double [C]cure; save from [**]wrath and [G]make me [C]pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Not the [**]labors [F]of my [C]hands, can ful[G]fill Thy law's de[C]mands
Could my [G]zeal no [G7]respite [C]know, could my [G]tears for[G7]ever [C]flow
All for [C]sin could [F]not a[C]tone; Thou must [**]save, and [G]Thou a[C]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Nothing [C]in my [F]hand I [C]bring, simply [G]to the cross I [C]cling
Naked, [G]come to [G7]Thee for [C]dress; helpless, [G]look to [G7]Thee for [C]grace
Foul, I [C]to the [F]fountain [C]fly; wash me, [**]savior, [G]or I [C]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C]While I [**]draw this [F]fleeting [C]breath, when mine [G]eyes shall close in [C]death
When I [G]soar to [G7]worlds un[C]known, see Thee [G]on Thy [G7]judgment [C]throne
Rock of [C]Ages, [F]cleft for [C]me, let me [**]hide my[G]self in [C]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
